Register offsets and bit meanings used by observe.c are facts taken, read-only,
from m1n1 src/pcie.c (sources/m1n1-baseline, SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT,
Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors): APCIE_PHY_CTRL 0x000 (CLK0/1 REQ/ACK,
RESET_T8103 bit7), APCIE_PHYIF_CTRL 0x024 (RUN), APCIE_PORT_LINKSTS 0x208
(UP, BUSY, L2), APCIE_PORT_APPCLK 0x800 (EN), APCIE_PORT_STATUS 0x804 (RUN),
APCIE_PORT_RESET 0x814 (DIS). The PMGR guard words and predicates are the
lab's own m1-dart-survey guard. No m1n1, Linux or Apple code is copied here.
board.c and survey.h are the lab's frozen m1-dart-survey files, used unchanged.
